# A raised-cosine offset: the shorter the bend, the larger the radiation loss.
# Reference: the same propagation stepped independently in NumPy. The pipeline checks that transmission rises with length.
title S-bend shifting a 0.5 um guide by 1 um over 10 um
window width=24 length=30
guide straight x=0 width=0.5 from=0 to=10
guide sbend x0=0 x1=1 width=0.5 from=10 to=20
guide straight x=1 width=0.5 from=20 to=30
launch mode x=0 width=0.5
monitor out z=30 x=1 width=0.5
plane end z=30
expect power out 0.998061697 2e-7
expect total end 0.999999819 2e-7
expect centroid end 0.9933069 2e-6
expect radius end 0.2795752 2e-6
expect neff 2.633014842 2e-8
